<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacques Cartier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1491–1557</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacques Cartier was a French explorer who made voyages to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> from 1534. He explored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-st-lawrence">Gulf of St. Lawrence</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-lawrence-river">St. Lawrence River</a> and claimed the region for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. His expeditions are regarded as the beginning of French claims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and part of the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier.jpg" alt="Jacques Cartier" width="313" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Théophile Hamel / After François Nicholas Riss · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacques_Cartier_1851-1852.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
